Acceptance criteria:
Lighting is independently labeled and reachable with named 44px controls.
Moving or collapsing console tools does not move or hide lighting. Lamp,
Room and Pear Boy continue changing the existing actual scene state, including
Pear brightness and Escape dismissal. GBA/DS selection and play/Inspect/table
retain shared settings. Both docks fit supported desktop, portrait-phone and
landscape sizes without overlapping each other; mobile inspection controls
remain below lighting. Whole-player fullscreen retains the lighting dock.
No native input, runtime, renderer, light/shader, quality, deadline, retry or
deployment-gate changes. Technical qualification is not owner acceptance.

Completion evidence:
Implementation changes HTML/CSS only; existing app IDs/handlers are retained.
Browser coverage observes actual imported scene state, independent main-dock
movement/collapse, real fullscreen and physical DS power reachability.
Responsive capture readiness requires the current renderer dimensions and a
completed natural room paint, rather than only potentially stale DOM anchors.
